IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc25-alternative-measures`

-- ccc25-tests-alternative-measures.l4 -- tests for sections 715.44 to 715.6 (src lines 15039 to 15169).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, with the words that decide it.

§ `Section 715.44 -- definitions`
-- 15040: alternative measures means measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act that are applicable in respect of a person who is 18 years of age or older and is alleged to have committed an offence. Arguments: other than judicial proceedings; applicable in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence; the person's age in years.
#ASSERT `s 715.44 alternative measures` TRUE TRUE 18 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 18 years of age: the boundary, "18 years of age or older"
#ASSERT `s 715.44 alternative measures` TRUE TRUE 40 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- older than 18
#ASSERT `s 715.44 alternative measures` TRUE TRUE 17 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- under 18: the means-definition says no
#ASSERT `s 715.44 alternative measures` FALSE TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- judicial proceedings are not alternative measures
#ASSERT `s 715.44 alternative measures` TRUE FALSE 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not applicable in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence
-- 15041: restorative justice, in respect of the criminal justice system, means an approach to justice that seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships.
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an approach to justice that seeks to repair the harm
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not an approach to justice in respect of the criminal justice system
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- does not seek to repair the harm caused by an offence
-- 15042: a process that provides an opportunity ... to communicate, directly or indirectly, about the causes, circumstances and impacts of an offence or alleged offence in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused.
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice process` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice process` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: it is a process
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice process` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: an opportunity to communicate
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice process` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: about causes, circumstances and impacts
#ASSERT `s 715.44 restorative justice process` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- missing: in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm

§ `Sections 715.45 and 715.46 -- purpose and principles`
-- 15053-15057: the following principles apply to this Part: (a) to (d).
#ASSERT `s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` `s 715.46(a) judicial resources are more appropriately used in relation to offences that pose a risk to the safety of the public` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` `s 715.46(b) measures that are taken under this Part allow for effective and timely intervention focused on addressing the circumstances underlying the offence or alleged offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` `s 715.46(c) crime has a harmful impact on victims and on society and measures that are taken under this Part should take into consideration their interests` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` `s 715.46(d) measures that are taken under this Part take into account the personal circumstances and characteristics of the person alleged to have committed the offence or of the offender and of the victim, as the case may be, with particular attention to the needs of Aboriginal persons and Black persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (d)
#ASSERT `s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` `s 715.46 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other statement: the list is not closed

§ `Sections 715.47 and 715.48 -- warnings and referrals`
-- 15061-15064 (1): a police officer must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, ... consider, instead of proceeding with the laying of an information, (a) taking no further action; (b) issuing a warning; (c) with the consent of the person, referring them. Arguments: the option; appropriate in the circumstances; poses a risk to the safety of the public.
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(a) taking no further action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- option (a), appropriate and no risk
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(a) taking no further action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not appropriate in the circumstances: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(a) taking no further action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- poses a risk to the safety of the public: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(b) issuing a warning to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- option (b), appropriate and no risk
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(b) issuing a warning to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not appropriate in the circumstances: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(b) issuing a warning to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- poses a risk to the safety of the public: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- option (c), appropriate and no risk
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not appropriate in the circumstances: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1)(c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- poses a risk to the safety of the public: the duty does not arise (the text's "if")
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1) an option that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an option the paragraphs do not name: not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` `s 715.47(1) an option that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the duty does not arise at all, whatever the option
-- 15066 (2): the failure of a police officer to consider the options does not invalidate any subsequent charges. Arguments: the officer failed to consider; the charges are subsequent charges against the person for the offence.
#ASSERT `s 715.47(2) the failure of the police officer to consider the options invalidates the subsequent charges` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not invalidate": the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.47(2) the failure of the police officer to consider the options invalidates the subsequent charges` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no failure to consider: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.47(2) the failure of the police officer to consider the options invalidates the subsequent charges` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not subsequent charges for the offence: outside the subsection
-- 15068-15070 (1): a prosecutor must, if it is appropriate and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, ... consider, before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings, (a) issuing a warning; (b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an alternative measure. Arguments: the option; before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings; appropriate; poses a risk.
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(a) issuing a warning to the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- option (a), appropriate and no risk
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(a) issuing a warning to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not appropriate in the circumstances
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(a) issuing a warning to the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- poses a risk to the safety of the public
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(a) issuing a warning to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- option (b), appropriate and no risk
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not appropriate in the circumstances
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- poses a risk to the safety of the public
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1)(b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` `s 715.48(1) an option that neither paragraph (a) nor (b) names` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an option the paragraphs do not name: not covered
-- 15072 (2): the failure of a prosecutor to consider the options does not invalidate any proceedings against the person for the offence.
#ASSERT `s 715.48(2) the failure of the prosecutor to consider the options invalidates the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not invalidate": the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.48(2) the failure of the prosecutor to consider the options invalidates the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no failure: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.48(2) the failure of the prosecutor to consider the options invalidates the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other proceedings: outside the subsection

§ `Sections 715.49 to 715.52 -- alternative measures`
-- 15078-15085: alternative measures may be used ... if the following conditions are met: (a) to (g). Field order: (a) authorized program; (b) person considering is satisfied it is appropriate; (c) fully and freely consents; (d) advised of the right to counsel; (e) accepts responsibility; (f) sufficient evidence in the opinion of the Attorney General or agent; (g) prosecution not barred at law.
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- all seven conditions met
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (a) authorized program not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (b) satisfied it is appropriate not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (c) fully and freely consents not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (d) advised of the right to counsel not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (e) accepts responsibility not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (f) sufficient evidence not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
#ASSERT `s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` (`s 715.49 what the facts show` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- condition (g) not barred at law not met: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (not "may not")
-- 15089-15091: alternative measures must not be used in respect of a person who (a) denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence; or (b) expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court. Arguments: denies; expresses the wish.
#ASSERT `s 715.5 alternative measures must not be used in respect of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) denies
#ASSERT `s 715.5 alternative measures must not be used in respect of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) wishes the charge dealt with by the court
#ASSERT `s 715.5 alternative measures must not be used in respect of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- both
#ASSERT `s 715.5 alternative measures must not be used in respect of the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither: the bar's own wording does not reach this person, not covered
-- 15093: no admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure is admissible in evidence against that person in any civil or criminal proceedings.
#ASSERT `s 715.51 the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an admission made as a condition of an alternative measure, offered against the person
#ASSERT `s 715.51 the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility: outside the section
#ASSERT `s 715.51 the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made as a condition of an alternative measure: outside the section
#ASSERT `s 715.51 the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not offered against that person: outside the section
-- 15095 (1): the use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act.
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1) the use of alternative measures is a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "is not a bar": the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1) the use of alternative measures is a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no alternative measures used: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1) the use of alternative measures is a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not proceedings under this Act: outside the subsection
-- 15095-15096 (1)(a): in the case where a charge is laid, if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied, the court must dismiss the charge. Arguments: a charge is laid; the court is satisfied of total compliance.
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(a) the court must dismiss the charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- charge laid and total compliance
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(a) the court must dismiss the charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the case where a charge is laid": none laid
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(a) the court must dismiss the charge` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied of total compliance: the duty of (a) does not arise
-- 15095-15097 (1)(b): in the case where a charge is laid, if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied, the court may dismiss the charge if, in the opinion of the court, the prosecution would be unfair. Arguments: a charge is laid; satisfied of partial compliance; unfair in the court's opinion.
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- all three
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "in the case where a charge is laid": none laid (a "where" gate: listed, JUST FALSE by the periods ruling)
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not satisfied of partial compliance: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the court does not think the prosecution unfair: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither: not covered
-- 15099 (2): subject to subsection (1), nothing in this Part is to be construed as preventing any person from laying an information, obtaining the issue or confirmation of any process or proceeding with the prosecution of any offence, in accordance with the law. Arguments: the act; done in accordance with the law; subsection (1)(a) requires dismissal.
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) laying an information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- nothing in this Part prevents it
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) obtaining the issue or confirmation of any process` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- nothing in this Part prevents it
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) proceeding with the prosecution of any offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- nothing in this Part prevents it
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) an act that none of those names` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another act: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) laying an information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in accordance with the law: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` `s 715.52(2) proceeding with the prosecution of any offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsection (1)": the dismissal of (1)(a) prevails, so the subsection does not answer

§ `Sections 715.53 and 715.54 -- restorative justice processes`
-- 15105-15112: the following additional principles apply to the use of restorative justice processes: (a) to (g).
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(a) restorative justice processes prioritize the acknowledgement and acceptance of responsibility for the harm caused to victims and communities and the repair of that harm by the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(c) they take into consideration the safety and security of all participants and seek to prevent further harm` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(d) they are based on courtesy, compassion and respect, including respect for the dignity of all participants` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (d)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(e) they foster and support the meaningful participation of those affected, including victims, persons alleged to have committed an offence and offenders and their communities` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (e)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(f) they enable participants to communicate openly and honestly and to have an active role in determining how to address their needs, as they perceive them` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (f)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53(g) they provide opportunities for understanding, healing and change and contribute to the restoration and recovery of victims and the rehabilitation and reintegration of persons alleged to have committed an offence or offenders` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed principle (g)
#ASSERT `s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` `s 715.53 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (g) names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other statement: the list is not closed
-- 15107 (b): participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time.
#ASSERT `s 715.53(b) the participant must fully and freely consent to participate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a participant
#ASSERT `s 715.53(b) the participant must fully and freely consent to participate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a participant: outside the principle
#ASSERT `s 715.53(b) the participant may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a participant may freely withdraw at any time
#ASSERT `s 715.53(b) the participant may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a participant: outside the principle
-- 15114 (1): A restorative justice process may be used at any stage of a criminal justice process, including as an alternative measure.
#ASSERT `s 715.54(1) a restorative justice process may be used at the stage` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- any stage of a criminal justice process
#ASSERT `s 715.54(1) a restorative justice process may be used at the stage` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a stage of a criminal justice process: outside the grant's own wording
-- 15116 (2): a restorative justice process may take various forms, including a mediation or dialogue, a restorative conference or a sentencing circle.
#ASSERT `s 715.54(2) a restorative justice process may take the form` `s 715.54(2) a mediation or dialogue between the victim and the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- mediation or dialogue
#ASSERT `s 715.54(2) a restorative justice process may take the form` `s 715.54(2) a restorative conference` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- restorative conference
#ASSERT `s 715.54(2) a restorative justice process may take the form` `s 715.54(2) a sentencing circle` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- sentencing circle
#ASSERT `s 715.54(2) a restorative justice process may take the form` `s 715.54(2) a form that none of those names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "including": another form is not covered
-- 15118 (3): for greater certainty, sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply when a restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part. Arguments: the provision (section as a decimal; 715.5 is section 715.5); used as an alternative measure.
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.49, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.49 is within 715.49 to 715.52, and the process is used as an alternative measure
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.5, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.5 is within 715.49 to 715.52, and the process is used as an alternative measure
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.51, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.51 is within 715.49 to 715.52, and the process is used as an alternative measure
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.52, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.52 is within 715.49 to 715.52, and the process is used as an alternative measure
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.49, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "when ... used as an alternative measure": it is not (fork F13)
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.5, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "when ... used as an alternative measure": it is not (fork F13)
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.48, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 715.48 is outside 715.49 to 715.52
#ASSERT `s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.53, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 715.53 is outside 715.49 to 715.52

§ `Section 715.55 -- conferences`
-- 15122 (1): a judge, justice or any person authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3) may convene or cause to be convened a conference. Arguments: the person (a Party); the person is authorized under the rules and practices.
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` `a judge` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a judge
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` `a justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a justice
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` `the clerk of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a person authorized under the rules and practices of subsection (3)
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` `the clerk of the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a judge, a justice or a person so authorized: not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` `the accused` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not covered
-- 15122 (1): a conference, in which a prosecutor, a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender, and any other person who could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2), participate. Arguments: the person; the person could assist with the objectives.
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `the prosecutor` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `the accused` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- a person alleged to have committed an offence
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `the offender` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an offender
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `a witness` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- any other person who could assist with the objectives
#ASSERT `s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` `a witness` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person who could not assist: not covered
-- 15124 (2): the objective of a conference is, among other things, to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes and to make recommendations.
#ASSERT `s 715.55(2) the objective is an objective of a conference` `s 715.55(2) to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence or the offender` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- first named objective
#ASSERT `s 715.55(2) the objective is an objective of a conference` `s 715.55(2) to make recommendations, if appropriate, in respect of resolution options, treatment plans, counselling and health and social services` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- second named objective
#ASSERT `s 715.55(2) the objective is an objective of a conference` `s 715.55(2) an objective that neither of those names` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "among other things": another objective is not covered
-- 15126 (3): the Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province may establish rules and practices ... other than for conferences convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice. Arguments: the person is the Attorney General or a designated minister; the conference is convened by a judge or justice.
#ASSERT `s 715.55(3) the person may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of the conference` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the Attorney General, a conference not convened by a judge or justice
#ASSERT `s 715.55(3) the person may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of the conference` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "other than for conferences convened ... by a judge or justice": the text excludes them
#ASSERT `s 715.55(3) the person may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of the conference` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- excluded in the text's own words, whoever asks
#ASSERT `s 715.55(3) the person may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of the conference` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Attorney General or a designated minister: not covered
-- 15128 (4): in provinces and territories where rules and practices are established under subsection (3), the conferences to which those rules and practices apply must be convened and conducted in accordance with them. Arguments: rules are established; they apply to the conference.
#ASSERT `s 715.55(4) the conference must be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- rules established and applicable
#ASSERT `s 715.55(4) the conference must be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where rules and practices are established": none established
#ASSERT `s 715.55(4) the conference must be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the conferences to which those rules and practices apply": these rules do not apply to it

§ `Sections 715.56 to 715.6 -- records`
-- 15132: sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48. Arguments: the provision (section 715.6 is the decimal 715.6, which comes after 715.59); the person has been issued a warning or referral.
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.57, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.57 is within 715.57 to 715.6; a warning or referral was issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.57, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral": none issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.58, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.58 is within 715.57 to 715.6; a warning or referral was issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.58, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral": none issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.59, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.59 is within 715.57 to 715.6; a warning or referral was issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.59, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral": none issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.6, "") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- section 715.6 is within 715.57 to 715.6; a warning or referral was issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.6, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral": none issued
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.56, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 715.56 is outside 715.57 to 715.6
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 715.49, "") FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 715.49 is outside 715.57 to 715.6
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 716, "") FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 716 is above 715.6, outside 715.57 to 715.6
#ASSERT `s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` (`Provision of the Code` OF 716, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 716 is above 715.6, outside 715.57 to 715.6, whether or not a warning was issued
-- 15134: the police officer who issues a warning or makes a referral is to keep a record.
#ASSERT `s 715.57 the police officer is to keep a record of the warning issued or referral made, including the identity of the person warned or referred` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the officer who issued a warning or made a referral
#ASSERT `s 715.57 the police officer is to keep a record of the warning issued or referral made, including the identity of the person warned or referred` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another person: outside the section
-- 15136 (1): a record relating to any offence alleged to have been committed by a person may be kept by any police force responsible for, or participating in, the investigation of the offence. Arguments: a record relating to an offence alleged to have been committed; the force is responsible for or participating in the investigation.
#ASSERT `s 715.58(1) the record may be kept by the police force` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- such a record, such a force
#ASSERT `s 715.58(1) the record may be kept by the police force` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not such a record: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.58(1) the record may be kept by the police force` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a force not responsible for or participating in the investigation: not covered
-- 15138 (2): a peace officer may disclose to any person any information in a record kept under this section that is necessary to disclose in the conduct of the investigation of an offence. Arguments: the information is in a record kept under 715.58; necessary to disclose in the conduct of the investigation.
#ASSERT `s 715.58(2) a peace officer may disclose the information to any person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- kept under this section and necessary
#ASSERT `s 715.58(2) a peace officer may disclose the information to any person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in a record kept under this section: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.58(2) a peace officer may disclose the information to any person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not necessary for the investigation: not covered
-- 15140 (3): a peace officer may disclose to an insurance company any information in a record kept under this section for the purpose of investigating any claim arising out of an offence. Arguments: in a record kept under 715.58; the disclosure is to an insurance company for that purpose.
#ASSERT `s 715.58(3) a peace officer may disclose the information to an insurance company` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- to an insurance company for the purpose of investigating a claim
#ASSERT `s 715.58(3) a peace officer may disclose the information to an insurance company` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in a record kept under this section: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.58(3) a peace officer may disclose the information to an insurance company` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another recipient or purpose: not covered
-- 15142-15145 (1): a department or agency of any government in Canada may keep records containing information obtained (a) for an investigation; (b) for use in proceedings under this Act; (c) as a result of the use of alternative measures. Arguments: why the information was obtained; the holder is a department or agency.
#ASSERT `s 715.59(1) the department or agency may keep records containing the information` `s 715.59(1)(a) for the purposes of an investigation of an offence alleged to have been committed by a person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed reason (a)
#ASSERT `s 715.59(1) the department or agency may keep records containing the information` `s 715.59(1)(b) for use in proceedings against a person under this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed reason (b)
#ASSERT `s 715.59(1) the department or agency may keep records containing the information` `s 715.59(1)(c) as a result of the use of alternative measures to deal with a person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- listed reason (c)
#ASSERT `s 715.59(1) the department or agency may keep records containing the information` `s 715.59(1) for a reason that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another reason: not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.59(1) the department or agency may keep records containing the information` `s 715.59(1)(a) for the purposes of an investigation of an offence alleged to have been committed by a person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a department or agency of a government in Canada: outside the subsection
-- 15147 (2): any person or organization may keep records containing information obtained as a result of the use of alternative measures.
#ASSERT `s 715.59(2) the person or organization may keep records containing the information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- information obtained as a result of the use of alternative measures
#ASSERT `s 715.59(2) the person or organization may keep records containing the information` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other information: outside the subsection
-- 15149-15159 (1): information in a record kept under 715.57 to 715.59 may be made available to (a) a judge or court; (b) a peace officer; (c) a member of a government department or agency; (d) any other person deemed by a judge to have a valid interest, to the extent directed by the judge, if the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is (i) desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes, or (ii) desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice. Arguments: the recipient; the record is kept under 715.57 to 715.59; the judge is satisfied under (d)(i); the judge is satisfied under (d)(ii).
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(a) any judge or court, for any purpose relating to proceedings relating to offences committed or alleged to have been committed by the person to whom the record relates` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named recipient (a) any 
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(a) any judge or court, for any purpose relating to proceedings relating to offences committed or alleged to have been committed by the person to whom the record relates` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the record is not kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(b)(i) any peace officer, for the purpose of investigating any offence that the person is suspected on reasonable grounds of having committed, or in respect of which the person has been arrested or charged` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named recipient (b)(i) a
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(b)(i) any peace officer, for the purpose of investigating any offence that the person is suspected on reasonable grounds of having committed, or in respect of which the person has been arrested or charged` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the record is not kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(b)(ii) any peace officer, for any purpose related to the administration of the case to which the record relates` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named recipient (b)(ii) 
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(b)(ii) any peace officer, for any purpose related to the administration of the case to which the record relates` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the record is not kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(c)(i) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is engaged in the administration of alternative measures in respect of the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named recipient (c)(i) a
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(c)(i) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is engaged in the administration of alternative measures in respect of the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the record is not kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(c)(ii) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is preparing a report in respect of the person as required under this Act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named recipient (c)(ii) 
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(c)(ii) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is preparing a report in respect of the person as required under this Act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the record is not kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d): the judge is satisfied under (i)
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d): the judge is satisfied under (ii)
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1)(d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- (d): the judge is not satisfied: the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered (fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` `s 715.6(1) a recipient that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another recipient: not covered
-- 15161 (2): information contained in the record, other than the identity of the person, may be made available to a member of a department or agency engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures. Arguments: the information is other than the identity; the recipient is so engaged.
#ASSERT `s 715.6(2) the information may be made available to the recipient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- other than the identity, to such a recipient
#ASSERT `s 715.6(2) the information may be made available to the recipient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the identity itself: the text does not say (fork F15)
#ASSERT `s 715.6(2) the information may be made available to the recipient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another recipient: outside the subsection
-- 15163 (3): if a record is made available for inspection to any person under (1)(d)(i), that person may subsequently disclose information contained in the record but may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person. Arguments: made available under (1)(d)(i); disclosed in an identifying form.
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may subsequently disclose the information contained in the record` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- made available under (1)(d)(i), not in an identifying form
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may subsequently disclose the information contained in the record` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify": the text says no
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may subsequently disclose the information contained in the record` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made available under (1)(d)(i): the grant's "if" gate fails, not covered
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may subsequently disclose the information contained in the record` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not made available under (1)(d)(i): outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may not disclose the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may not disclose the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a form that would not identify: the bar's own wording does not reach it
#ASSERT `s 715.6(3) the person may not disclose the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a person to whom a record was made available under (1)(d)(i): outside the subsection (fork F30)
-- 15165 (4): any person to whom a record is authorized to be made available under this section may be given any information contained in the record and a copy of any part of it.
#ASSERT `s 715.6(4) the person may be given the information contained in the record and a copy of any part of the record` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- authorized to have the record made available
#ASSERT `s 715.6(4) the person may be given the information contained in the record and a copy of any part of the record` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not so authorized: outside the subsection
-- 15167 (5): evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral, evidence that a police officer has taken no further action and evidence of the offence are inadmissible for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour in any proceedings before a court in respect of the individual. Arguments: the evidence; offered to prove prior offending behaviour; in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual.
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named evidence, offered to prove prior offending behaviour
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- offered for another purpose: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named evidence, offered to prove prior offending behaviour
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- offered for another purpose: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence of the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- named evidence, offered to prove prior offending behaviour
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence of the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- offered for another purpose: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence of the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` `s 715.6(5) evidence that none of those names` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other evidence: outside the subsection
-- 15169 (6): a record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59 may not be introduced into evidence, except for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c), more than two years after the end of the period during which the alternative measure was applied. Arguments: the record is so kept; the introduction is for the purposes of 721(3)(c); the day of the introduction; the day the period ended.
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE FALSE (Date 16 6 2028) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one day more than two years after the end of the period
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE FALSE (Date 15 6 2028) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exactly two years after: not "more than" two years, the bar does not yet apply
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE FALSE (Date 14 6 2028) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- less than two years after: the bar does not yet apply
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE TRUE (Date 16 6 2028) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "except for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)": the exception
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` FALSE FALSE (Date 16 6 2028) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a record kept under 715.57 to 715.59: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- period ended 29 February 2024: two years on is read as 28 February 2026 (fork F11), so 1 March 2026 is more than two years after
#ASSERT `s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` TRUE FALSE (Date 28 2 2026) (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 28 February 2026 is the second anniversary read that way: not more than two years after

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.47 to 715.58, run with #TRACE`
-- Each trace is expected to end as the comment above it says. Where the text states no time limit the rule has no WITHIN, so an act not done leaves a standing obligation, never a breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.47(1) the police officer's duty to consider the options` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 715.47(1) consider taking no further action, issuing a warning, or referring the person` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.47(1) the police officer's duty to consider the options` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor's duty to consider the options` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the prosecutor` DOES `s 715.48(1) consider issuing a warning or referring the person` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.48(1) the prosecutor's duty to consider the options` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the duty is performed)
#TRACE `s 715.52(1)(a) the court's duty to dismiss the charge` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 715.52(1)(a) dismiss the charge` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING   (no time limit is stated, so the duty stays open)
#TRACE `s 715.52(1)(a) the court's duty to dismiss the charge` AT 0 WITH

-- EXPECT FULFILLED   (the permission is performed)
